**Given:**

A man covers the first half of the journey at the speed of 60 km/h and the remaining at the speed of 84 km/h.

**Formula used:**

Average speed = dfrac{2 times S₁ times S₂}{S₁ + S₂}

Where, S₁ = speed for the first half, S₂ = speed for the second half

**Calculations:**

Average speed = dfrac{2 times 60 times 84}{60 + 84}

⇒ Average speed = dfrac{2 times 60 times 84}{144}

⇒ Average speed = 70 km/h

∴ The correct answer is option (1).

